liation was verified from the repository. Show the real maintainer name; do not substitute an account portrait, identicon, or engine logo.","Access type","pipeline source","access","section",[75],{"_58":76,"_25":64,"_77":78},"Pipeline source","note","Published generator implementation and prompts; this is not a complete release of every benchmark game.","video","demo",[82],{"_58":83,"_25":84,"_77":85},"Unity generation video","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xyJjFfnxUx0","Author-linked demonstration video, not a browser-playable game.","tutorial",[88],{"_58":89,"_25":90,"_77":91},"Installation and usage","https://github.com/yxwan123/UniGen#-installation","README covers prerequisites and the local Unity generation workflow; review paths and project setup before running.","Source reviewed","2026-10-18","verified","metadata","Year","2025","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[105],"dimensions","3D","Development stages",[109,110,111,112],"stages","Planning","Gameplay & code","Engines & scenes","Testing","Topics",[116,117,118,119],"tags","Unity","Game generation","Scene assembly","Research prototype","Further reading",[122],{"_58":123,"_25":124},"Paper","https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.26161","Project source",[127],{"_58":125,"_25":64},"Why it belongs here","A multi-agent research workflow for Unity game creation from natural-language descriptions. The repository publishes its Python pipeline and model connector, with installation guidance and a recorded demonstration. Unity and a model-service account are required. Public pipeline code is available, but a hosted playable build and complete downloadable versions of the benchmark games were not verified.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Framework","Category","3D development","category","lead","summary","name","3d","framework",[156],{"_86":152,"_80":153,"_32":154},[116,117,118,119],[148,149,150,151],[140],2025,"plan","code","scene","test",{"_58":89,"_25":90,"_17":86,"_77":91},{"_58":83,"_25":84,"_17":79,"_77":85},{"_58":